# Lobby is read-only and Object is not.  The Lobby prototype carries the
# `lobbies` registry that the runtime maintains on every realm create and
# free; a script reshaping it would corrupt session management for every
# other lobby.  Extending Object, by contrast, is a documented idiom.
#
# So a slot write to Lobby raises, and the throw reaches the client as a
# runtime error rather than being swallowed.

## mode: repl

> {"id":12,"op":"eval","code":"Lobby.forbidden = 99"}
< "id":12 | "kind":"error" | "code":"runtime"
< "id":12 | "kind":"done"
